(5502779, 791693, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: made me lol, so an automatic 8, had I voted.<br/> <br/>Technical: Comp is pleasing, DOF is very shallow, there''s a little glare to the left, the lampshade vanishes against the bg.  Some oof clutter in bg...but...<br/> <br/>Artistic: Lots of fun and work went into this shot, don''t think it wasn''t noticed and appreciated! Love the phone off the hook and the painting in the bg. Obviously the voters liked it, finished in the top 20.  Well done!<br/> <br/>FWIW: I would''ve tried to get the chair in focus, to emphasize the scale, and left the hand as is.  All in all a fun shoot, definitely got across the whole concept of Miniature very well!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-05-27 18:22:27.</i></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: made me lol, so an automatic 8, had I voted. Technical: Comp is pleasing, DOF is very shallow, there''s a little glare to the left, the lampshade vanishes against the bg.  Some oof clutter in bg...but... Artistic: Lots of fun and work went into this shot, don''t think it wasn''t noticed and appreciated! Love the phone off the hook and the painting in the bg. Obviously the voters liked it, finished in the top 20.  Well done! FWIW: I would''ve tried to get the chair in focus, to emphasize the scale, and left the hand as is.  All in all a fun shoot, definitely got across the whole concept of Miniature very well! Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-05-27 19:20:33.000000', '2009-05-27 19:22:27.000000', 0),
(5502798, 791597, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: Ooh, wish I''d shot this...<br/> <br/>Technical: Great use of thirds, dof great, lovely lighting, but if this is simply a long shot of Mount Hood (I thought it was Mount Baker at first) then sadly it is DNMC.  But...<br/> <br/>Artistic: It is still a very good photo and pleasing to the eye.  Can''t figure out what the crop (as in veggies) is in the foreground; hopefully something legal! :-)<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: Ooh, wish I''d shot this... Technical: Great use of thirds, dof great, lovely lighting, but if this is simply a long shot of Mount Hood (I thought it was Mount Baker at first) then sadly it is DNMC.  But... Artistic: It is still a very good photo and pleasing to the eye.  Can''t figure out what the crop (as in veggies) is in the foreground; hopefully something legal! :-) Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-05-27 19:28:54.000000', NULL, 0),
