(5505090, 791781, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: looks very much like the kind of shot I would do...or attempt anyway :-)<br/> <br/>Technical: Composition quite good, the eye goes straight to the vase and tiny flowers which are all nicely in focus.  I like that the rose itself is oof, adds some depth, and macros can often look too flat.  Needs a little more light coming in from behind the rose to knock out that unlit area and help kill shadows underneath, maybe help backlight it a bit to give it a glow.  Almost some glare on the white petals of the toy flowers, but looks like you erred on the side of caution.  Another f-stop up and you probably would have had glare.<br/> <br/>Artistic: very simple and sweet shot, certainly meets the challenge description and you finished with a respectable score.<br/> <br/>Overall a very decent entry, good work and look forward to seeing more!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions.<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: looks very much like the kind of shot I would do...or attempt anyway :-) Technical: Composition quite good, the eye goes straight to the vase and tiny flowers which are all nicely in focus.  I like that the rose itself is oof, adds some depth, and macros can often look too flat.  Needs a little more light coming in from behind the rose to knock out that unlit area and help kill shadows underneath, maybe help backlight it a bit to give it a glow.  Almost some glare on the white petals of the toy flowers, but looks like you erred on the side of caution.  Another f-stop up and you probably would have had glare. Artistic: very simple and sweet shot, certainly meets the challenge description and you finished with a respectable score. Overall a very decent entry, good work and look forward to seeing more! Feel free to PM me with any questions. Susan', '2009-05-29 19:51:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(5505106, 791532, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: I get tipsy just looking at it :-) would have got a 7 from me in voting because I like the atmosphere here, very cozy and warm.<br/> <br/>Technical: Lighting looks ambient and 6 seconds...wow, you really wanted to get the most out of it, esp as you shot at f4.  Seems to have been worth it.  Tiny little higlights work well too, could well have been glare-y.  Comp very simple, but some may not have cared for the chair and fern in the b/g.<br/> <br/>Artistic: Hmm...curved table top or truly tilted?  Either way i think the slight list is fun and adds to the shot.  Like the slight blur/double lettering in the reflection of the JD bottle for same reason.<br/> <br/>FWIW: The chair in the b/g may have put some voters off, if they thought it was making the comp cluttered.  I do find my eye wandering up the curve of the large bottle to the fern, thence to the easy chair.  Just for fun, re-do this pic and black out the chair and fern, see how it changes your shot.  Note that I didn''t say doing so would necessarily improve your shot; that is your call to make.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: I get tipsy just looking at it :-) would have got a 7 from me in voting because I like the atmosphere here, very cozy and warm. Technical: Lighting looks ambient and 6 seconds...wow, you really wanted to get the most out of it, esp as you shot at f4.  Seems to have been worth it.  Tiny little higlights work well too, could well have been glare-y.  Comp very simple, but some may not have cared for the chair and fern in the b/g. Artistic: Hmm...curved table top or truly tilted?  Either way i think the slight list is fun and adds to the shot.  Like the slight blur/double lettering in the reflection of the JD bottle for same reason. FWIW: The chair in the b/g may have put some voters off, if they thought it was making the comp cluttered.  I do find my eye wandering up the curve of the large bottle to the fern, thence to the easy chair.  Just for fun, re-do this pic and black out the chair and fern, see how it changes your shot.  Note that I didn''t say doing so would necessarily improve your shot; that is your call to make. Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-05-29 20:19:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5505115, 791804, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: OMG I have to critique one of Don''s pix, I not only have to make it sound like I know what I''m talking about, it also won the brown...!  But this shot does grow on you.<br/> <br/>Technical: Comp OK, lighting is ambient, maybe ap open a little more to 1/100 or so and f-stop one or two higher.  Just a teeny-tiny itty-bitty bit oof.<br/> <br/>Artistic: Very impressionistic, the dead leaves and blurry b/g give it a sense of surreality. Does that make sense? Actually the glowy blur does make the bug''s wings look somewhat ethereal.  Quite nice.<br/> <br/>Overall: Ummm....err....*scratching head* I actually cannot think of a way to improve upon this shot.  Well done! :-)<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: OMG I have to critique one of Don''s pix, I not only have to make it sound like I know what I''m talking about, it also won the brown...!  But this shot does grow on you. Technical: Comp OK, lighting is ambient, maybe ap open a little more to 1/100 or so and f-stop one or two higher.  Just a teeny-tiny itty-bitty bit oof. Artistic: Very impressionistic, the dead leaves and blurry b/g give it a sense of surreality. Does that make sense? Actually the glowy blur does make the bug''s wings look somewhat ethereal.  Quite nice. Overall: Ummm....err....*scratching head* I actually cannot think of a way to improve upon this shot.  Well done! :-) Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-05-29 20:33:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(5505170, 791804, 57229, '<td valign="top">You snuck in for the brown - congrats...</td>', 'You snuck in for the brown - congrats...', '2009-05-29 21:34:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5505603, 790600, 5169, '<td valign="top">*Greetings from the Critique Club*<br/> <br/>I hope the best for the baby hedgehogs. What I can read from this photo is the helplessness of an abandoned new born.<br/> <br/>Composition:<br/> <br/>The leaning head to the right gives it a nice perspective.  Hedgehogs are kind of "hate" or "love" kind of creatures. Depth of field in this photo is very low. A well focused image would have glorified the hedgehog''s bristles (their main peculiarity). <br/> <br/>One last thing to consider is that the challenge calls for photographs that show the idea of miniature.  This photograph eludes that principle but it is saved by the title. What could you have done to show the true size of this creature? Some kind of contrast object in the composition could have helped this photograph to accomplish the challenge theme even without the explicit title.<br/> <br/>Keep up the good work!<br/> <br/>Alex<br/> <br/></td>', '*Greetings from the Critique Club* I hope the best for the baby hedgehogs. What I can read from this photo is the helplessness of an abandoned new born. Composition: The leaning head to the right gives it a nice perspective.  Hedgehogs are kind of "hate" or "love" kind of creatures. Depth of field in this photo is very low. A well focused image would have glorified the hedgehog''s bristles (their main peculiarity).  One last thing to consider is that the challenge calls for photographs that show the idea of miniature.  This photograph eludes that principle but it is saved by the title. What could you have done to show the true size of this creature? Some kind of contrast object in the composition could have helped this photograph to accomplish the challenge theme even without the explicit title. Keep up the good work! Alex ', '2009-05-30 11:34:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(5506057, 791760, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: Often seen this view from a plane, too, so yes everything is very teeny from way up there.  Having said that, this would be a shoehorn, as the scale presents the boat as miniature...but it isn''t a true miniature.  You often have to interpret the challenge very literally to do well.<br/> <br/>Technical: POV and comp interesting, but shot quite grainy. Feel that the b/w doesn''t do this shot justice, even muted colours may have helped it pop a little more.<br/> <br/>Artistic: I like the clouds casting shadows on the mountains towards the middle/right of shot, gives it depth and texture.<br/> <br/>Overall: Not a bad effort, you have the right approach.  Keep shooting!<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: Often seen this view from a plane, too, so yes everything is very teeny from way up there.  Having said that, this would be a shoehorn, as the scale presents the boat as miniature...but it isn''t a true miniature.  You often have to interpret the challenge very literally to do well. Technical: POV and comp interesting, but shot quite grainy. Feel that the b/w doesn''t do this shot justice, even muted colours may have helped it pop a little more. Artistic: I like the clouds casting shadows on the mountains towards the middle/right of shot, gives it depth and texture. Overall: Not a bad effort, you have the right approach.  Keep shooting! Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-05-30 20:34:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(5506067, 791822, 59029, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>Initial impression: Very cute, almost expect to see a Jimmy Carter ref in there too :-0<br/> <br/>Technical: Slightly busy in terms of composition; find it hard to locate the focal point, eye roves around too much.  Ambient lighting fine, a little drab perhaps.  Would look to see this closed down an f-stop or two, maybe slow the shutter to 1/80.  On a personal level I think you relied a little too much on post-processing; on this site, you must still have a good, clean shot to work with.  All the pp in the world will not help a poor shot.<br/> <br/>Artistic: As already noted, the gravel in the upper left area distracts the eye from the scene in the foreground.  <br/> <br/>Overall: A good try, reminds me of my early days here - feel free to look at my first few dozen entries or so, they''ll make you feel better. :-)  Keep shooting, that''s the only way to go.<br/> <br/>Feel free to PM me with any questions,<br/> <br/>Susan</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! Initial impression: Very cute, almost expect to see a Jimmy Carter ref in there too :-0 Technical: Slightly busy in terms of composition; find it hard to locate the focal point, eye roves around too much.  Ambient lighting fine, a little drab perhaps.  Would look to see this closed down an f-stop or two, maybe slow the shutter to 1/80.  On a personal level I think you relied a little too much on post-processing; on this site, you must still have a good, clean shot to work with.  All the pp in the world will not help a poor shot. Artistic: As already noted, the gravel in the upper left area distracts the eye from the scene in the foreground.   Overall: A good try, reminds me of my early days here - feel free to look at my first few dozen entries or so, they''ll make you feel better. :-)  Keep shooting, that''s the only way to go. Feel free to PM me with any questions, Susan', '2009-05-30 20:52:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(5506495, 791663, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/> <br/>I am sorry that this image did not score a bit higher for you in the miniature challenge.  I personally thought it met the challenge topic very well.<br/> <br/>From a technical point of view, the mini tea pot is quite out of focus which I do not think is very helpful when trying to score high in these challenges.  Other things that have likely contributed to a lower score are the background and the border.<br/> <br/>It was mentioned already in the comments made during the challenge that the background was somewhat distracting, and I do have to agree with this.  A plain background would likely have worked much better.<br/> <br/>Then we come to the border.  I have observed that heavy borders such as the one you have used here, hurt rather than help scores here on DPC.  Typically a border should enhance the overall image presentation and in this case, I do not really believe it does.  Something a little less in your face may have worked better.  <br/> <br/>At the end of the day, I still gave this a 6 as I felt the subject worked well in this challenge. A better focus would undoubtedly have increased my score.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club I am sorry that this image did not score a bit higher for you in the miniature challenge.  I personally thought it met the challenge topic very well. From a technical point of view, the mini tea pot is quite out of focus which I do not think is very helpful when trying to score high in these challenges.  Other things that have likely contributed to a lower score are the background and the border. It was mentioned already in the comments made during the challenge that the background was somewhat distracting, and I do have to agree with this.  A plain background would likely have worked much better. Then we come to the border.  I have observed that heavy borders such as the one you have used here, hurt rather than help scores here on DPC.  Typically a border should enhance the overall image presentation and in this case, I do not really believe it does.  Something a little less in your face may have worked better.   At the end of the day, I still gave this a 6 as I felt the subject worked well in this challenge. A better focus would undoubtedly have increased my score. ', '2009-05-31 12:33:11.000000', NULL, 0),
(5506504, 790198, 62357, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>Interesting take on this challenge.  Technically the shot is well composed, lighting is good, it''s in focus etc, so all good from that point of view.<br/> <br/>I believe the primary reason it did not score higher was down to the inclusion of the computer monitor in the background.  I personally am struggling with the relevance of this as in my opinion it spoils what is quite a good image.<br/> <br/>I''m afraid I gave it a fairly low score, due to the background.  Would have been considerably higher without the computer there.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. Interesting take on this challenge.  Technically the shot is well composed, lighting is good, it''s in focus etc, so all good from that point of view. I believe the primary reason it did not score higher was down to the inclusion of the computer monitor in the background.  I personally am struggling with the relevance of this as in my opinion it spoils what is quite a good image. I''m afraid I gave it a fairly low score, due to the background.  Would have been considerably higher without the computer there.', '2009-05-31 12:41:37.000000', NULL, 0),
